1410
00:59:05.570 --> 00:59:07.730
screenings and doctor's appointments.

1411
00:59:07.930 --> 00:59:10.250
But luckily, I went when I did.

1412
00:59:10.490 --> 00:59:13.090
My cancer was found early and it was treatable.

1413
00:59:13.270 --> 00:59:17.110
But if I had waited a few months longer, things could have been way worse.

1414
00:59:18.010 --> 00:59:23.830
And caught early, many cancers have survival rates well over 90%.

1415
00:59:23.830 --> 00:59:28.090
However, most people don't prioritize their recommended screenings.

1416
00:59:28.090 --> 00:59:32.370
And one of the biggest reasons why is because they can't get time off work.

1417
00:59:32.930 --> 00:59:37.930
So that's why I'm trying to get the word out about the Screening Time Off program, which

1418
00:59:37.930 --> 00:59:44.690
encourages employees to take time to step out for screenings by asking employers to join

1419
00:59:44.690 --> 00:59:50.510
Screening Time Off to take the pledge that you will let your employees off to get these

1420
00:59:50.510 --> 00:59:51.130
